<h2 id="flat-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="057N">38.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
In this chapter, we discuss some advanced results on flat modules and flat morphisms of schemes and applications. Most of the results on flatness can be found in the paper <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/GruRay">GruRay</a>]</span> by Raynaud and Gruson. 
</p>
<p>
Before reading this chapter we advise the reader to take a look at the following results (this list also serves as a pointer to previous results): 
</p>
<ol>
  <li><p>
General discussion on flat modules in Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00H9" data-tag="00H9">10.39</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The relationship between $\text{Tor}$-groups and flatness, see Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00LY" data-tag="00LY">10.75</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Criteria for flatness, see Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00MD" data-tag="00MD">10.99</a> (Noetherian case), Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/051E" data-tag="051E">10.101</a> (Artinian case), Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00R3" data-tag="00R3">10.128</a> (non-Noetherian case), and finally More on Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/039A" data-tag="039A">37.16</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Generic flatness, see Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/051Q" data-tag="051Q">10.118</a> and Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/0529" data-tag="0529">29.28</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Openness of the flat locus, see Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/00R8" data-tag="00R8">10.129</a> and More on Morphisms, Section <a href="/tag/0398" data-tag="0398">37.15</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Flattening, see More on Algebra, Sections <a href="/tag/0521" data-tag="0521">15.16</a>, <a href="/tag/05LJ" data-tag="05LJ">15.17</a>, <a href="/tag/05LK" data-tag="05LK">15.18</a>, <a href="/tag/05LN" data-tag="05LN">15.19</a>, and <a href="/tag/05LV" data-tag="05LV">15.20</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Additional results in More on Algebra, Sections <a href="/tag/052Y" data-tag="052Y">15.21</a>, <a href="/tag/0549" data-tag="0549">15.22</a>, <a href="/tag/054A" data-tag="054A">15.26</a>, and <a href="/tag/0535" data-tag="0535">15.27</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>
 As applications of the material on flatness we discuss the following topics: a non-Noetherian version of Grothendieck's existence theorem, blowing up and flatness, Nagata's theorem on compactifications, the h topology, blow up squares and descent, weak normalization, descent of vector bundles in positive characteristic, and the local structure of perfect complexes in the h topology. 
</p>
